lines_added: 120
decisions:
  - id: video-frame-provider-injection
    decision: VideoFrameProvider is an injected callback in RenderOptions, not a global singleton
    rationale: Mirrors the ImageCache injection pattern — keeps canvas package environment-agnostic and allows swapping preview (HTMLVideoElement) vs export (WebCodecs/Mediabunny) providers without touching renderer code
  - id: videometa-on-asset-now
    decision: Added videoMeta to Asset in Phase 1 rather than deferring
    rationale: Makes ^valid-video-layer gate load-bearing (can actually check sourceEnd ≤ duration) rather than decorative — advisor explicitly flagged decorative gates as an antipattern
  - id: startframe-as-temporal-anchor
    decision: startFrame on VideoVisual controls when the clip begins in composition time
    rationale: Video clips need an explicit clip-in point in composition space; all other layer temporal presence is controlled via opacity deltas, but that model doesn't suit video which starts decoding from a specific source offset
errors_encountered:
  - description: VideoVisual not exported from packages/types/src/index.ts
    resolution: Added VideoVisual to the export list in index.ts
    time_to_fix: 1 min
  - description: VideoFrameProvider return type used DOM globals (HTMLVideoElement, ImageBitmap, HTMLCanvasElement) which canvas package excludes from tsconfig
    resolution: Changed return type to object | null with JSDoc explaining runtime types
    time_to_fix: 2 min
